window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-d2a5e4aaee788341"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"discover-protein-folding-models\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">探索蛋白质折叠模型</h1> <p>将蛋白质折叠假设转化为经过基准测试的实验循环。</p> <p>使用 Codex 的 Goal Mode 研究并实现对 AlphaFold2 的新架构改动，以提升蛋白质折叠表现。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>针对可自动评分的基准，探索架构、损失函数或训练课程改动的计算生物学家。</li> <li>有明确科学假设、希望缩短从想法到可运行实验分支路径的研究人员。</li> <li>需要持久实验跟踪和迭代调试的机器学习工程师，他们会运行长期自主研究循环。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">起步提示词</h2> <p>运行由科学家指导的架构搜索</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">使用 Goal Mode，在 NanoFold 公共基准上提升这款 AlphaFold2 风格蛋白质结构模型的验证集 lDDT-Cα 分数。\n\n科学假设是：持续保留高阶几何状态，可能帮助模型在有限数据条件下更有效地学习蛋白质几何结构：\n\n- 保留标准的 MSA 和成对表示；\n- 为选定的残基三元组添加稀疏的可学习 2-simplex 面状态；\n- 为选定的残基四元组添加稀疏的可学习 3-simplex 四面体状态；\n- 只根据官方基准输入和模型生成的循环复用几何结构构建拓扑；\n- 在 NanoFold 约束下，让实现保持实际可计算。\n\n请持续维护以下跟踪文件：\n\n1. 在 PLAN.md 中记录当前策略、状态和拟议的后续步骤\n2. 在 EXPERIMENTS.md 中用结构化日志记录实验和结果\n3. 在 EXPERIMENT_NOTES.md 中持续记录临时笔记和想法\n\n每轮迭代：\n\n1. 说明要检验的假设；\n2. 做最小且连贯的代码或配置改动；\n3. 运行相关测试和一小部分基准测试；\n4. 记录指标、延迟、内存和失败模式；\n5. 决定保留、撤销还是细化这项改动；\n6. 定期重新评估架构层面的搜索方向，而不只是调整局部超参数。\n\n不要根据冒烟测试或单条链的过拟合诊断声称模型具备泛化提升。优先做条件匹配的比较，并保留证据适用范围的边界。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/use-cases/follow-goals\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">跟进目标（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/SimplexFold\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SimplexFold 代码库（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/SimplexFold/blob/main/BENCHMARK_PLAN.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SimplexFold 基准测试计划（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/nanoFold-Competition\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">NanoFold 竞赛（需联网）</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>如需完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"explore-a-protein-folding-architecture-hypothesis\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">探索蛋白质折叠架构假设</h2> <p>如果某个蛋白质折叠假设需要多轮实现，Goal Mode 就很适合这种任务。为 Codex 提供一个范围明确的科学方向、可用的基线，以及可自动评分的基准。Codex 可以实现架构分支、跟踪实验、诊断失败，并在你审阅证据的同时继续迭代。</p> <p>这个示例从一个具体问题开始：如果 AlphaFold2 风格模型的主干不仅表示残基和残基对，也显式表示更高阶的拓扑对象，它是否能更有效地学习蛋白质几何结构？</p> <p><a id=\"define-a-bounded-experiment\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">定义边界清楚的实验</h2> <p>AlphaFold2 已在 Evoformer 中使用强大的成对推理和三角推理。三角运算能够改进边表示，但仍会将结果写回成对张量。科学家提出，在数据有限的情况下，持续保留可学习的三角面和四面体单元表示，是否能提供有用的归纳偏置。</p> <p>由此产生的公开代码库 <a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/SimplexFold\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SimplexFold（需联网）</a>，在传统成对表示 <code>Z_ij</code> 之外，添加了稀疏面状态 <code>F_ijk</code> 和四面体状态 <code>U_ijkl</code>。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">MSA representation M\n        &lt;-&gt; pair / edge tensor Z_ij\n        &lt;-&gt; sparse face tensor F_ijk\n        &lt;-&gt; sparse tetra tensor U_ijkl\n        -&gt; structure module\n        -&gt; recycled geometry\n        loops back into the next pass\n</code></pre> <p>从本页的起始提示词、最小 AlphaFold2 风格基线和公开 NanoFold 基准开始。该基准提供了规模小、经过整理、数据固定且可自动评分的底座，可用于结构生物学实验。第一版实现应保持足够小，以便在启动昂贵的训练之前，先通过有针对性的单元测试和微基准测试进行检验。</p> <p><a id=\"run-the-search-with-goal-mode\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"goal-mode\">使用 Goal Mode 运行搜索</h2> <ol> <li>提供一个可证伪的高层科学假设，而不是让模型从零编造整套研究计划。</li> <li>在 ChatGPT 中使用 GPT-5.5 Pro，将这一研究方向转化为含有明确约束和消融实验的实现计划。</li> <li>要求 Codex 实现最小且可运行的 <a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/SimplexFold\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SimplexFold（需联网）</a> 基线，然后通过有针对性的单元测试和微基准测试验证它。</li> <li>将生成的代码库交给 Codex Goal Mode，让它在 NanoFold 基准上逐步提升验证集 <code>lDDT-Cα</code>，同时保留实验日志、计划和产物引用。</li> <li>让 Goal Mode 持续运行，根据基准反馈迭代架构、训练方案和实验框架。此示例中的循环运行了 150 多个小时。</li> </ol> <p>用 <code>PLAN.md</code> 记录当前策略和后续步骤，用 <code>EXPERIMENTS.md</code> 结构化记录结果，并用 <code>EXPERIMENT_NOTES.md</code> 持续记录笔记。这些产物能让长时间运行的搜索过程可审计，也为你提供一个稳定的位置来调整后续方向。</p> <p>Goal Mode 适用于需要反复实现、测试、跟踪实验、诊断失败并由基准驱动迭代的搜索。无引导的自主研究往往会偏向熟悉的局部改动，例如损失函数、优化器和超参数。由科学家提供的精炼假设可以形成更有意义的搜索空间，同时仍为测试、诊断和细化留出余地。</p> <p>这种工作流也适用于团队评估：科学家参与引导会如何影响代理式科学搜索的质量。</p> <p><a id=\"example-result\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">示例结果</h2> <p>该流程产生了 <a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/SimplexFold\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SimplexFold（需联网）</a>——一种显式表示高阶 simplex 状态的实验性架构。请将拓扑结构与基准测试日志放在一起审阅，确认后续每轮仍在检验原始科学设想。</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">1-simplex、2-simplex 和 3-simplex 蛋白质几何结构的比较。 · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/discover-protein-folding-architectures-simplex.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>1-simplex、2-simplex 和 3-simplex 蛋白质几何结构的比较。 · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/discover-protein-folding-architectures-simplex.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">打开官网原始媒体</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>有价值的结论并不是“Codex 自主解决了蛋白质折叠问题”。这个工作流展示的是：Goal Mode 可以构成一个持续的科学工程循环——科学家提出关键概念方向，代理则压缩实现、实验、调试和后续搜索的周期。</p> <p>把有希望的诊断结果视为实现路径可行的证据，而不是泛化能力的证明。定期审阅代理的轨迹；如果它偏离到局部超参数调节，应将其引回有科学意义的架构问题；只有在匹配的公开验证比较和适当重复实验通过后，才应提升相关结论的可信度。</p> <p><a id=\"resources\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">资源</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/SimplexFold\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SimplexFold 代码库（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/SimplexFold/blob/main/BENCHMARK_PLAN.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SimplexFold 基准测试计划（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/nanoFold-Competition\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">NanoFold 竞赛（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/nanoFold-Competition/blob/main/docs/COMPETITION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">NanoFold 竞赛规则（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://x.com/ChrisHayduk/status/2055757345506877759?s=20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Goal Mode 连续运行 150 多小时（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://x.com/ChrisHayduk/status/2053807198870880743?s=20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Goal Mode 文章（需联网）</a></li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"discover-protein-folding-models\">Discover protein folding models</h1> <p>Turn protein-folding hypotheses into benchmarked experiment loops.</p> <p>Use Codex with Goal Mode to research and implement novel architectural modifications to AlphaFold2 for improved protein folding performance.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Computational biologists exploring architecture, loss, or curriculum changes against an automatically scorable benchmark.</li> <li>Researchers who have a scientifically motivated hypothesis and want to compress the path from idea to working experimental fork.</li> <li>ML engineers running long-lived autoresearch loops that require persistent experiment tracking and iterative debugging.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Run a Scientist-guided Architecture Search</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>high</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use Goal Mode to improve the validation lDDT-Cα score of this AlphaFold2-style protein-structure model on the NanoFold public benchmark.\n\nThe scientific hypothesis is that persistent higher-order geometric states may help the model learn protein geometry more efficiently from limited data:\n\n- retain the standard MSA and pairwise representations;\n- add sparse learned 2-simplex face states for selected residue triplets;\n- add sparse learned 3-simplex tetrahedral states for selected residue quadruplets;\n- construct topology only from official benchmark inputs and model-generated recycled geometry;\n- keep the implementation computationally practical under NanoFold constraints.\n\nMaintain durable tracking files for:\n1. The current strategy, status, and proposed next steps in PLAN.md\n2. A structured log of experiments and results in EXPERIMENTS.md\n3. A running scratchpad of notes and thoughts in EXPERIMENT_NOTES.md\n\nFor each iteration:\n1. state the hypothesis being tested;\n2. make the smallest coherent code or configuration change;\n3. run the relevant tests and benchmark slice;\n4. record metrics, latency, memory, and failure modes;\n5. decide whether to keep, revert, or refine the change;\n6. periodically reassess the architecture-level search direction rather than only tuning local hyperparameters.\n\nDo not claim generalization gains from smoke tests or single-chain overfit diagnostics. Prefer matched comparisons and preserve the evidence boundary.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/codex/use-cases/follow-goals\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Follow a goal (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/SimplexFold\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SimplexFold repository (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/SimplexFold/blob/main/BENCHMARK_PLAN.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SimplexFold benchmark plan (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/nanoFold-Competition\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">NanoFold competition (online)</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"explore-a-protein-folding-architecture-hypothesis\">Explore a protein-folding architecture hypothesis</h2> <p>Use Codex Goal Mode when you have a protein-folding hypothesis that needs more than one implementation pass. Give Codex a bounded scientific direction, a working baseline, and an automatically scorable benchmark. Codex can implement the architecture fork, track experiments, diagnose failures, and continue iterating while you review the evidence.</p> <p>This example started with a specific question: could an AlphaFold2-style model learn useful protein geometry more efficiently if its trunk represented not only residues and residue pairs, but also explicit higher-order topological objects?</p> <h2 id=\"define-a-bounded-experiment\">Define a bounded experiment</h2> <p>AlphaFold2 already uses powerful pairwise and triangle-style reasoning inside the Evoformer. Its triangle operations improve edge representations, but still write back into a pair tensor. The scientist proposed testing whether persistent learned representations for triangular faces and tetrahedral cells could provide a useful inductive bias in a data-limited setting.</p> <p>The resulting public repository, <a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/SimplexFold\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SimplexFold (online)</a>, adds sparse face states <code>F_ijk</code> and tetrahedral states <code>U_ijkl</code> alongside the conventional pair representation <code>Z_ij</code>.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">MSA representation M\n        &lt;-&gt; pair / edge tensor Z_ij\n        &lt;-&gt; sparse face tensor F_ijk\n        &lt;-&gt; sparse tetra tensor U_ijkl\n        -&gt; structure module\n        -&gt; recycled geometry\n        loops back into the next pass\n</code></pre> <p>Start with the starter prompt on this page, a minimal AlphaFold2-style baseline, and the public NanoFold benchmark. The benchmark provides a small, curated fixed-data and automatically scorable substrate for structural-biology experimentation. Keep the first implementation small enough to test with targeted unit tests and microbenchmarks before launching expensive training runs.</p> <h2 id=\"run-the-search-with-goal-mode\">Run the search with Goal Mode</h2> <ol> <li>Supply a falsifiable, high-level scientific hypothesis instead of asking the model to invent an entire research agenda from scratch.</li> <li>Use GPT-5.5 Pro in ChatGPT to convert that direction into an implementation plan with explicit constraints and ablations.</li> <li>Ask Codex to implement the smallest runnable <a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/SimplexFold\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SimplexFold (online)</a> baseline, then verify it with targeted unit tests and microbenchmarks.</li> <li>Give the resulting repository to Codex Goal Mode and instruct it to hill-climb validation <code>lDDT-Cα</code> on the NanoFold benchmark while preserving experiment logs, plans, and artifact references.</li> <li>Run Goal Mode continuously while it uses benchmark feedback to iterate on the architecture, training recipe, and experimental harness. In this example, the loop ran for more than 150 hours.</li> </ol> <p>Use <code>PLAN.md</code> for the current strategy and next steps, <code>EXPERIMENTS.md</code> for a structured log of results, and <code>EXPERIMENT_NOTES.md</code> for the running scratchpad. These artifacts make a long-running search auditable and give you a stable place to steer the next iteration.</p> <p>Goal Mode is useful here because the search requires repeated implementation, testing, experiment tracking, failure diagnosis, and benchmark-driven iteration. Unguided autoresearch often drifted toward familiar local changes such as losses, optimizers, and hyperparameters. A compact scientist-supplied architecture hypothesis gave Codex a more meaningful search space while still leaving room to test, diagnose, and refine the implementation.</p> <p>This workflow is also useful for teams evaluating how scientist-in-the-loop steering changes the quality of agentic scientific search.</p> <h2 id=\"example-result\">Example result</h2> <p>The result of this workflow was <a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/SimplexFold\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SimplexFold (online)</a>, an experimental architecture with explicit higher-order simplex states. Review the topology alongside the benchmark logs to confirm that each iteration still tests the original scientific idea.</p> <figure> <p class=\"media-note\">A comparison of 1-, 2-, and 3-simplex protein geometry. · <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/discover-protein-folding-architectures-simplex.webp\">联网查看原始媒体</a></p> <figcaption>A comparison of 1-, 2-, and 3-simplex protein geometry. · <a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/discover-protein-folding-architectures-simplex.webp\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open original media</a></figcaption> </figure> <p>The useful lesson is not that Codex autonomously solved protein folding. The workflow shows how Goal Mode can act as a persistent scientific engineering loop: a scientist contributes the conceptual move, and Codex compresses the implementation, experimentation, debugging, and follow-up search cycle.</p> <p>Treat promising diagnostics as evidence that the implementation path works, not as proof of generalization. Review the agent's trajectory periodically, steer it back toward scientifically meaningful architecture questions if it collapses into local hyperparameter tuning, and promote claims only after matched public-validation comparisons and appropriate replicates.</p> <h2 id=\"resources\">Resources</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/SimplexFold\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SimplexFold repository (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/SimplexFold/blob/main/BENCHMARK_PLAN.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SimplexFold benchmark plan (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/nanoFold-Competition\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">NanoFold competition (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://github.com/ChrisHayduk/nanoFold-Competition/blob/main/docs/COMPETITION.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">NanoFold competition rules (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://x.com/ChrisHayduk/status/2055757345506877759?s=20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Goal Mode running for more than 150 hours (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://x.com/ChrisHayduk/status/2053807198870880743?s=20\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Goal Mode article (online)</a></li> </ul>"};
